{{Quote|I'm a full fan every single day I go to work. Everyone's like, “We're all just fans going to work, making ''Star Wars''.” It sounds so over the top for me to say what I'm about to say, but I truly mean it. In my life, when I'm facing a challenge, I just think about the general spirit of the franchise and taking on challenges with a bit of positivity, a bit of humor and then being able to move on. So it's just been something that I have learned a lot from, as I'm playing the role itself.|Natasha Liu Bordizzo discussing playing Sabine Wren in ''Ahsoka''|<ref name="Day Shift" />}}
'''Natasha Liu Bordizzo''' is an [[Wikipedia:Australians|Australian]] [[Wikipedia:Actor|actress]] who portrays [[Sabine Wren]] in the [[2023]] television series ''[[Star Wars: Ahsoka]]''.

==Biography==
When Natasha Liu Bordizzo was filming the movie [[Wikipedia:Day Shift (film)|''Day Shift'']], she filmed a self-tape in which she played a male [[pilot]] in a scene from [[Wikipedia:Top Gun|''Top Gun'']]. In another scene, her character was paid by a lady to help her, and her line was "Hey lady, I've got all these problems, so stop bothering me. All the work is moving south for the winter." Bordizzo was not given any information on what the audition was for, but she assumed it was for a project with [[Jon Favreau]]. She then sent the tape and did not hear anything for a few weeks. Bordizzo later got a call asking if she likes ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]'' and she said she did. Months later, Bordizzo met<ref name="Day Shift" /> ''[[Star Wars: Ahsoka]]'' executive producers<ref name="Announcement">{{SW|url=news/future-lucasfilm-projects-revealed|text=Future Lucasfilm Projects Revealed}}</ref> [[Dave Filoni]] and Favreau, and the latter explained that he tried to make the casting process as smooth as possible.<ref name="Day Shift" />

After Bordizzo was cast as the [[Mandalorian]] [[Sabine Wren]] in the series<ref name="Day Shift" /> in [[2021]],<ref name="Natasha Rosario SWCA">{{SWYouTube|8RZiIf_oEAc|Rosario Dawson and Natasha Liu Bordizzo takes the stage at SWCA 2022 &#124; Star Wars Celebration Live!}}</ref> Filoni and Favreau told her it would be great if she watched ''[[Star Wars Rebels]]'', but they said the live-action version would always be a new thing that finds its own truth. Bordizzo watched the show because she felt obligated, and she found it to be a free preparation. She liked how Wren showed bravery and spirit despite the challenges and heartache she faced.<ref name="Day Shift" /> She had a hard time keeping it a secret. Bordizzo and [[Rosario Dawson]], the actress who played [[Ahsoka Tano]], received [[Wikipedia:Chinese martial arts|wushu]] training from stunt coordinator [[Ming Qiu]].<ref name="Natasha Rosario SWCA" /> Bordizzo decided to not take a course in [[Wikipedia:Aerosol paint|spray painting]] because she felt Wren would experiment with it.<ref name="Day Shift" /> At the Mando+ panel at [[Celebration Anaheim (2022)|Celebration Anaheim]], [[2022]], it was announced that Bordizzo would play Wren in ''Ahsoka''.<ref name="MandoPlus" />

